      "message": "The semantics of `lcp_router_route_mk_mprefix()` were modified in another recent change so that it returns a boolean now if the address length was too long. The return value should be checked and we should return without doing anything if it returns false. It would probably be better to do this early in the function. E.g. change the `if (!lcp_router_route_mk_prefix(rr, \u0026pfx))` at line 1393 to\n```\n  if (!lcp_router_route_mk_prefix(rr, \u0026pfx) || (rtype \u003d\u003d RTN_MULTICAST \u0026\u0026 !lcp_router_route_mk_mprefix(rr, \u0026mpfx)))\n  ```",
      "revId": "ec9dd1f8e8816372a431c67a58460995d3a2eb13",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
